{
  "slug": "artist:a-ap-rocky",
  "name": "A$AP Rocky",
  "editorial_article": "Born Rakim Athelston Mayers in Harlem, A$AP Rocky gained widespread attention in 2011 after his self-produced single 'Peso' leaked online, triggering a high-profile bidding war. He joined the A$AP Mob collective in 2007, an influential Harlem-based crew co-founded by A$AP Yams, A$AP Bari, and A$AP Illz. His debut mixtape 'Live. Love. A$AP' arrived in 2011 under the Polo Grounds Music and RCA Records umbrella. Rocky's studio work often utilizes distinct production collaborators, including Clams Casino, Danger Mouse, and Metro Boomin. His 2013 debut album 'Long. Live. A$AP' topped the Billboard 200, followed by subsequent number-one records including 2015's 'At. Long. Last. A$AP' and his 2026 project 'Don't Be Dumb'. Beyond his music, he founded the creative agency AWGE in 2014, bridging the gap between hip-hop and high fashion through collaborations with labels like JW Anderson and brands such as Puma. His career is marked by his evolution from a cloud rap pioneer in the early 2010s to a global cultural figure, balancing his work as a rapper, actor, and creative director for various commercial campaigns.",
